<h1>Head</h1>

<p class="l-ui-utility--mt-md">Use <code>content_for :l_ui_head</code> to inject content into the layout <code>&lt;head&gt;</code>, after the stylesheet. This is the right place for dynamic <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> blocks, preload hints, or other per-request head content.</p>

<h2 class="l-ui-utility--mt-2xl">Dynamic theme tokens</h2>

<p class="l-ui-utility--mt-md">Override CSS custom properties per request (e.g. per-tenant branding) by injecting a <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> block. Placing it after the stylesheet ensures the cascade override takes effect correctly.</p>

<pre class="l-ui-surface l-ui-utility--mt-lg"><code>&lt;% content_for :l_ui_head do %&gt;
  &lt;style&gt;
    :root { --accent: &lt;%= @tenant.accent_hsl %&gt;; --accent-foreground: 0 0% 100%; }
  &lt;/style&gt;
&lt;% end %&gt;</code></pre>

<p class="l-ui-notice--warning l-ui-utility--mt-lg"><strong>Security:</strong> never interpolate user-supplied strings directly into a <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> tag - this allows CSS injection. Validate or sanitise any user-derived values before interpolation.</p>

<p class="l-ui-utility--mt-lg">See the <%= link_to "colors", layout_colors_path %> page for the full list of design tokens.</p>

<h2 class="l-ui-utility--mt-2xl">CSP compatibility</h2>

<p class="l-ui-utility--mt-md">Inline <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> blocks are blocked by a strict <code>Content-Security-Policy: style-src 'self'</code> header. If your app enforces a strict CSP, add a nonce using Rails' <code>content_security_policy_nonce</code> helper - Rails includes the matching nonce in the CSP header automatically:</p>

<pre class="l-ui-surface l-ui-utility--mt-lg"><code>&lt;% content_for :l_ui_head do %&gt;
  &lt;style nonce="&lt;%= content_security_policy_nonce %&gt;"&gt;
    :root { --accent: &lt;%= @tenant.accent_hsl %&gt;; --accent-foreground: 0 0% 100%; }
  &lt;/style&gt;
&lt;% end %&gt;</code></pre>

<h2 class="l-ui-utility--mt-2xl">Turbo Drive compatibility</h2>

<p class="l-ui-utility--mt-md">With Turbo Drive, inline <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> blocks in <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> are not re-evaluated on navigation. Per-tenant tokens injected this way will persist stale after a Turbo page transition. To update tokens across navigations, either serve the theme as a server-side stylesheet URL or disable Turbo on affected links.</p>
